 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 507655,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which expression equals  <span data-math=\"{(x - y)}{(x - y)}\">{(x - y)}{(x - y)}</span>? Hint: Use the Distributive Property.<br>\n<span data-math=\"x^2-y^2\">x^2-y^2</span>\n<br>\n<span data-math=\"x^2 + y^2\">x^2 + y^2</span>\n<br>\n<span data-math=\" x^2-2xy-y^2\"> x^2-2xy-y^2</span>\n<br>\n<span data-math=\"x^2-2xy + y^2\">x^2-2xy + y^2</span>\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\left( {x - y} \\right)\\left( {x - y} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>Use the distributive property.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x\\left( {x - y} \\right) - y\\left( {x - y} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>Use the distributive property again.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x\\left( x \\right) - x\\left( y \\right) - y\\left( x \\right) - y\\left( { - y} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>Simplify.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"{x^2} - xy - xy + {y^2}\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"{x^2} - 2xy + {y^2}\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Two of the answers only have two terms, which is clearly wrong.</p>\n<p>One of the answers forgot that when you multiply a negative by a negative, the answer is a positive. It has the wrong sign on the squared <i>y</i> term.</p>\n<p>The correct answer is <span data-math=\"{x^2} - 2xy + {y^2}\"></span>.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{x^2}-2xy + {y^2}\">{x^2}-2xy + {y^2}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
